Algorithm
Start the program.
Create a graph using an adjacency list to represent locations and paths.
Accept the number of locations and paths from the user.
Add the paths between the locations to the graph.
Accept the starting location.
Apply DFS using recursion and display the exploration order.
Count and display the number of locations visited by DFS.
Apply BFS using a queue and display the exploration order.
Compare the DFS and BFS traversal orders.
Stop the program.
